              "text": "The Indiana Pacers **did not qualify for the 2026 NBA playoffs**. Plagued by major injuries\u2014including star guard Tyrese Haliburton missing the entire season after tearing his Achilles tendon in the 2025 Finals\u2014the Pacers finished near the bottom of the Eastern Conference with a 19\u201363 record. \n\nHowever, if you are looking for their opponents from their most recent playoff runs, the matchups are detailed below:\n\n### **2024\u201325 Playoffs (NBA Finals Run)**\nThe Pacers had a historic season, reaching the NBA Finals for the first time since 2000:\n*   **First Round:** Defeated the **Milwaukee Bucks** (4\u20131)\n*   **Conference Semifinals:** Defeated the **Cleveland Cavaliers** (4\u20131)\n*   **Conference Finals:** Defeated the **New York Knicks** (4\u20132)\n*   **NBA Finals:** Lost to the **Oklahoma City Thunder** (3\u20134)\n\n### **2023\u201324 Playoffs (Eastern Conference Finals Run)**\nThe Pacers surprised the league by making a deep postseason run as the 6th seed:\n*   **First Round:** Defeated the **Milwaukee Bucks** (4\u20132)\n*   **Conference Semifinals:** Defeated the **New York Knicks** (4\u20133)\n*   **Conference Finals:** Lost to the **Boston Celtics** (0\u20134)",
